==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|astronomy}} One day of [[solar time]]; the time in which a planet such as [[Earth]] apparently rotates once around its [[axis]] relative to the [[Sun]]; the time taken for the [[Sun]] to seem to be in the same place in the sky twice (on Earth about 24 hours as an average - the length of solar day is not constant throughout the year)

